/*

Exactly right. The two systems are completely independent:

						InpEquityProfitLock=false		InpEquityProfitLock=true
Existing profit lock	Follows InpProfitLock setting	Follows InpProfitLock setting
Equity profit lock		Skipped entirely				Activates immediately at trigger%

So there are four possible combinations:
InpEquityProfitLock		InpProfitLock		Behaviour		
false					false				No profit locking at all — original SL until BE/trail/cloud exit
false					true				Original R-based tier lock (activates after BE at 1.0R)
true					false				New equity lock only (activates immediately at trigger%)
true					true				Both active — equity lock fires first (before BE), R-based lock fires after BE

For your use case — you want the equity lock to protect small early profits — set:

InpEquityProfitLock = true
InpEPLTriggerPct   = 0.02   (0.02% of equity)
InpEPLLockPct      = 87.5   (lock 87.5% of profit)
InpProfitLock      = false  (don't need the R-based lock on top)

This gives you the immediate protection you described — as soon as profit reaches $20 on a $100k account, 87.5% is locked in and the SL trails continuously from there.

*/